      "text": "\\begin{align*}\nf(x) &= ax + b, \\\\\ng(f(x)) &= 2(ax + b) - 5, \\\\\n&= 2ax + 2b - 5, \\\\\ng(f(x)) &= 3x + 4,\n\\end{align*}\nTherefore, \\begin{align*} 2a &= 3, \\\\\n2b - 5 &= 4.\n\\end{align*} Solving these equations, we find $a=\\frac32$ and $b=\\frac92$ so $a+b=\\boxed{\\frac{15}{2}}$. The answer is \\frac{15}{2}",
